  "reviews": [
    {
      "author": "Nyanka",
      "content": "Just the right amount of cringey and cute\\~ &lt;3\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nAfter watching *Naughty Fukami* I was hesitant to give this one a shot, but since it's only about 2 hours of content there's not really a reason to not watch it. I was pleasantly surprised by how cute and funny this series was while also seriously discussing the problems that come from a relationship with a significant age gap. The actors did such a great job in their roles, Ai-chan was super cute without coming across as a helpless childish like some uke tend to do and Okumi-san was so fun and caring. Their intimacy scenes were all well done too, way better than *Naughty Fukami*. The actors seemed very comfortable around each other and looked like they were having fun acting together. I also really enjoyed all of the other characters, the side characters were able to add a more grounded feel to the series that is otherwise a bit outlandish. I really wish the series had been longer to really explore the setting and the relationship building, but for what it is, it's really good. If you're the type of fujoshi that really enjoyed reading smutty manga from the 2010s than you'll probably really enjoy this series too. My final rating is 8/10 stars.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nGeneral info for anyone wanting to know:\r\n\r\n• Is the series spicy/nsfw? Yes, the series shows full sex scenes (in almost every episode), but it doesn't show any nudity below the waist.\r\n\r\n• Is there noncon or violence? No.\r\n\r\n• Is there a love triangle? Yes/No, a second love interest for Ai-chan does pop up, but Ai-chan is never interested in him and tells him that point blank.",
      "rating": 8,
      "createdAt": "2026-09-07T18:27:58Z"
    }
